Z||000009||Rodney||05-13-2000||08:11 AM||||I do have a reasonable replacement speaker in stock. But more importantly I am having gaskets custom made to fit new speakers in the stock housings. In most if not all cases the new speaker will need to be mounted on the top of the original steel ring. This leaves a opening under the ring where the old speaker used to be. To retain the sealed enclosure design this area needs a gasket. I am having die cut gaskets custom made to fit this area. I am also having the original grate cover gasket reproduced. Should have a few prototypes in a week or so. If they look good I should have them available in 2-3 weeks. The gaskets will be available separately if you choose to use your own speaker. Until I have a batch run I will not know what the prices will be.<P>Rodney Dickman||||reg||1
